## Fleet SDD quick reference

Start any piece of work with `/sdd:next`. It reads the gate ledger and tells you
the stage, the artifact and the role that owns the blocking gate.

| Command | Does |
| --- | --- |
| `/sdd:next` | What is next, then do that role's work |
| `/sdd:role <id>` | Work as a named role regardless of stage |
| `/sdd:new "<title>"` | Scaffold a feature and start framing it |
| `/sdd:check` | Validate artifacts and gates |
| `/sdd:gate <id> [verdict]` | Review against the checklist, or record a verdict |
| `/sdd:status` | Every feature and what is blocking it |

The `sdd-review` skill reviews an artifact against the checklists of every role
that owns part of it — use it before a human signs a gate.

**Two things not to do:** never run `fleet-sdd gate ... approve` on a human's
behalf, and never delete a `TODO(sdd)` marker to make `check` pass.
